From 624fe20217cb85ea3b9b786b58a8008e20b763ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vasilii Zolotukhin <vasilii.zolotukhin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 09:31:44 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] Mac: Chrome-style profile switcher instead of AppKit's
 tab bar

AppKit's tab bar does not fit Chrome's UI, so it is hidden in every
window of the profile tab group. A tonal Material chip with the
profile's avatar and name sits right after the traffic lights; it takes
the profile's theme color and opens a menu of the open profile windows
(with their Ctrl+N shortcuts). The tab strip leaves room for it through
the existing caption exclusion, and a hit-test hook keeps clicks on the
chip from dragging the window. If AppKit's tab bar can't be hidden, the
previous "profile tabs on top" layout is used as a fallback.

Fullscreen is shared by the whole group, like native window tabs: AppKit
takes the group fullscreen and each profile window follows when it is
shown, so Ctrl+N switches profiles inside fullscreen. After a group was
fullscreen, AppKit tends to put windows straight into fullscreen at the
next launch; windows therefore can't be fullscreen-primary until they
have joined the group (or Chromium itself toggles fullscreen on them).
